\title{catmech: Auditable Model-Based Imputation and Category Sensitivity}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Auditable completion of a continuous measurement using Gaussian models, predictive mean matching, an explicitly measured internal reference subset, or a reference-calibrated contamination model of the recorded values. Supports flag masking, optional exact or fallible interval categories, posterior draws and per-record corruption probabilities, convergence and donor-support diagnostics, reference hold-out checks, finite-scenario sensitivity comparisons and 'mice' analysis adapters. Retains a separate retain-or-replace sensitivity engine. Implements multiple-imputation combining rules and finite-sample degrees of freedom following Rubin (1987) \doi{10.1002/9780470316696} and Barnard and Rubin (1999) \doi{10.1093/biomet/86.4.948}, and an unvalidated audit-size planning aid based on two-phase sampling theory (Neyman 1938) \doi{10.1080/01621459.1938.10503378}. Does not identify measurement error without assumptions or reference information, or guarantee coverage under misspecification.
}
